    {
      "type": 12,
      "content": {
        "version": "NotebookGroup/1.0",
        "groupType": "editable",
        "items": [
          {
            "type": 1,
            "content": {
              "json": "## About the data in this workbook\r\n\r\nThis workbook mixes two data sources on purpose, because neither one alone can\r\ncover an Azure AI estate.\r\n\r\n### What Azure Resource Graph can and cannot see\r\n\r\nMeasured against live fixtures, not assumed from ARM template documentation:\r\n\r\n| Resource type | Indexed in Resource Graph? |\r\n| --- | --- |\r\n| `microsoft.cognitiveservices/accounts` | **Yes** - fully, and verified to match the ARM control plane exactly |\r\n| `microsoft.cognitiveservices/accounts/projects` (Foundry projects) | **Yes** |\r\n| `microsoft.machinelearningservices/workspaces` (Hub / Project / ML) | **Yes** - rich properties |\r\n| `microsoft.cognitiveservices/accounts/deployments` (**model deployments**) | **No - zero rows. Not indexed at all.** |\r\n\r\nFor accounts, each of `identity.type`, `disableLocalAuth`, `publicNetworkAccess`,\r\n`restrictOutboundNetworkAccess`, `networkAcls.defaultAction`, `networkAcls.ipRules`,\r\n`allowProjectManagement` and `customSubDomainName` was **set through ARM and then\r\nre-read in Resource Graph** to confirm it round-trips. A blank value therefore means\r\n*not configured*, never *not indexed*.\r\n\r\n### How model data is retrieved\r\n\r\nBecause model deployments are invisible to Resource Graph:\r\n\r\n1. A Resource Graph query lists every in-scope Azure OpenAI / Foundry account.\r\n2. The Model deployments tab reads the selected account's ARM `/deployments`\r\n   endpoint directly, with one grid row per returned deployment.\r\n3. The Model retirement tab reads the regional model catalog\r\n   (`.../locations/{region}/models`) for live retirement dates and lifecycle status.\r\n\r\nThe deployments grid is deliberately not merged with the catalog: Workbooks exposes\r\nonly one join-column pair, and a composite JSONPath key can evaluate empty in some\r\nportal runtimes, turning the merge into a deployment-by-catalog cross join.\r\nRetirement dates are never hard-coded - they come from the catalog at query time.\r\n\r\n### How service retirement data is retrieved\r\n\r\nThe **Service retirements** tab keeps Service Health and Advisor as independent\r\nsources:\r\n\r\n1. `ServiceHealthResources` from Azure Resource Graph for subscription-specific\r\n   Health Advisory retirement events retained by Azure, including elapsed deadlines.\r\n2. `providers/Microsoft.Advisor/metadata` from the ARM control plane for Microsoft's\r\n   published Service Upgrade and Retirement metadata catalog from 2024 onward,\r\n   including elapsed and future dates.\r\n\r\nThe Service Health grid is filtered to AI-related retirement titles and summaries.\r\nThe Advisor summary covers AI, Data, Network, and Infrastructure metadata. Within\r\nthe Advisor section only, direct recommendation IDs are left-joined to resource\r\ncounts from `advisorresources`; row selection filters a separate affected-resources\r\ngrid below. Advisor metadata is a global planning catalog and does not by itself\r\nprove that a service is deployed in the selected scope.\r\n\r\n### Findings\r\n\r\n**Accounts** - API key auth enabled instead of Entra ID only; public network access\r\nwith no private endpoint; network ACLs allowing all traffic; no managed identity;\r\nno custom subdomain (which blocks Entra ID auth); Microsoft-managed keys instead of\r\nCMK; unrestricted outbound access; failed provisioning.\r\n\r\n**Workspaces** - public access with no private link; managed VNet isolation disabled;\r\ndatastores using access keys instead of identity; no CMK; no managed identity; soft\r\ndelete off; v1 legacy mode; project not linked to a hub; failed provisioning.\r\n\r\n| Severity | Condition |\r\n| --- | --- |\r\n| Critical | 6 or more findings |\r\n| High | 4-5 findings |\r\n| Medium | 2-3 findings |\r\n| Low | 1 finding |\r\n| Healthy | No findings |"
            },
            "name": "abHead"
          },
          {
            "type": 1,
            "content": {
              "json": "### Support and feedback\r\n\r\nFound an issue, a false positive, or a missing check? Please get in touch - detail\r\nwhich tab and which account or deployment is involved, and the fix will be turned\r\naround quickly.\r\n\r\n**Bulent Ozkir**\r\n[bulento@microsoft.com](mailto:bulento@microsoft.com) |\r\n[bulentozkir@hotmail.com](mailto:bulentozkir@hotmail.com)\r\n\r\n### License\r\n\r\nCopyright (c) 2026 Bulent Ozkir\r\n\r\nPermission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy of this\r\nsoftware and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal in the Software\r\nwithout restriction, including without limitation the rights to use, copy, modify,\r\nmerge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell copies of the Software, and to\r\npermit persons to whom the Software is furnished to do so, subject to the following\r\nconditions:\r\n\r\nThe above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all copies\r\nor substantial portions of the Software.\r\n\r\nTHE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED,\r\nINCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A\r\nPARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT\r\nHOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF\r\nCONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM, OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE\r\nOR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE SOFTWARE.",
              "style": "info"
            },
            "name": "abContact"
          }
        ]
